f  options to choose from and you obviously  want to choose wisely after unlocking  each base skill you can unlock three  upgrades for it be aware that only one  upgrade can be active at a time so have  a read of the options before you invest  some of the more useful ones I unlocked  early on where elven lights which  lines nearby enemies and it's upgrade  cleansing blaze which sets them all on  fire super handy for crowd control I  store minutes upgrade shower of ice  freezes all orcs in front of you perfect  counter and it's upgrade rain of arrows  allows you to refill one elf shot with a  perfectly timed counter now in the early  game you really don't have that many elf  shots so each one is precious and this  upgrade stops you from coming up short  detonate can help you make mischief from  afar as you can unleash a fiery  explosion or call in a group of spiders  or ghouls to swarm nearby enemies with  its upgrades poison tendril poisons a  grog barrel from a distance to damage  any orc the drinks from it and of course  the shadow strike allows you to reach  faraway enemies in a flash and move  around the battlefield with ease mounted  skills are also definitely worth  investing in as soon as you can  not only as some captain's afraid of  Kara Gore's they can take on a few  enemies on your behalf also there a  nifty way of getting from A to B number  3 upgrade your weapons enemy captains  and nemec's drop items upon defeat with  epic and legendary captain's dropping  back salute  there are various armor sets you can  collect and wear like the bright Lord  set you obtain by unlocking all the  elven doors each piece of epic and rare  gear has an Associated challenge  complete the challenge and pay a tiny  amount Mirian to upgrade your gear it  doesn't give you a whole lot more damage  and you can only upgrade an epic or rare  piece once but you can get some awesome  buffs like a certain percentage to  chance that an enemy's head will explode  and freak out others t